## Summary
The article discusses the paradigm shift toward remote working that began before the COVID-19 pandemic and has been accelerated by local and national directives. It emphasizes the importance of data protection in remote work environments, referencing the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).

## Key Points
- Remote working started gaining traction even before the COVID-19 pandemic.
- Pandemic-related directives have confined populations, increasing the prevalence of remote work.
- Data protection is a critical consideration in remote working setups to ensure security and compliance.
